  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\n_Apologies that I'm less familiar with the issue here than with #12209 - I came across an existing note in Ladybird's implementation, and realised we hadn't reported the issue. It's from 2024 so this may be entirely outdated but I thought it's better to report things just in case._\n\n---\n\nIn the [HTML fragment parsing algorithm](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/parsing.html#parsing-html-fragments), step 1 creates a temporary Document  \"`document`\", that is used for parsing.\n> 1. Let document be a Document node whose type is \"html\".\n\nIn 2024 we found that it was necessary to copy the context element's document's base URL to `document`, to prevent a crash with setting innerHTML on an element in a srcdoc iframe's document.\n\nLadybird commit where this was added, with some explanation: https://github.com/LadybirdBrowser/ladybird/commit/b64df59cc61f31b8a0aab91abb4630b3ecb1dcee",
